# CODEOWNERS: who GitHub asks to review a change.
# https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# The LAST matching pattern wins. Replace individual handles with a team
# (for example @GDG-TUM/ai-ml-track-leads) once the org has created one,
# so the file survives the next handover. See docs/maintainers-guide.md.

# Default: the track lead reviews everything
*                       @10kwise

# Governance, security and automation always need a lead
/GOVERNANCE.md          @10kwise
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md     @10kwise
/SECURITY.md            @10kwise
/.github/               @10kwise
/scripts/               @10kwise

# Content areas: add maintainers here as they join, for example:
# /weekly-sessions/     @10kwise @maintainer-handle
# /projects/            @10kwise @maintainer-handle
